// Rule: [T1127][T1036] Blinder Tunnel - MSBuild Runtimebrokers Runtimebroker
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1127, T1036
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Hunts MSBuild launching a masqueraded RuntimeBroker from a user-writable campaign path.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for msbuild runtimebrokers runtimebroker using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: A match supports the source-observed execution shape; it does not prove Blinder Tunnel attribution, DLL sideloading, C2, or successful compromise.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1127 (Trusted Developer Utilities Proxy Execution), T1036 (Masquerading)
// Classification: Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint / DeviceProcessEvents
// Evidence: Unit 42 observed msbuild.exe launching a renamed vshost.exe as
// RuntimeBroker.exe from %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\RuntimeBrokers.
// A match supports the source-observed execution shape; it does not prove
// Blinder Tunnel attribution, DLL sideloading, C2, or successful compromise.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where FileName =~ "RuntimeBroker.exe"
| where FolderPath contains @"\AppData\Local\Microsoft\RuntimeBrokers\"
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "msbuild.exe"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, AccountUpn, FileName, FolderPath,
          ProcessCommandLine, SHA1, ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, ProcessId, InitiatingProcessId,
          ProcessUniqueId, InitiatingProcessUniqueId, ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
